---
/* The clip shapes of the design, defined once per page.
 *
 * A `clip-path: url(#…)` resolves only against a definition in the *same*
 * document, so these travel with the layout rather than with whoever uses them:
 * forgetting them does not fail a build, it publishes an unclipped photo. A
 * guard checks that every reference in a published page finds its shape here.
 *
 * The geometry is the design's, copied from design-export/. The names are
 * Material 3's: an `id` is code, so the language rule wants it in English, and
 * rather than translating the Italian of the export by ear these take the name
 * Google gives the same geometry in its shape library — a shared vocabulary
 * instead of a private one.
 *
 *   f-quadrifoglio            → clip-clover-4      (4-leaf clover)
 *   f-esafoglio               → clip-cookie-6      (6-sided cookie)
 *   f-ottofoglio, m-ottofoglio → clip-clover-8     (8-leaf clover)
 *   f-gemma                   → clip-gem           (gem)
 *   f-obliqua                 → clip-slanted       (slanted)
 *
 * Five and not six: the export defines the eight-lobed shape twice, once per
 * file, because it is two designs — desktop and mobile — and this is one site.
 * The two definitions are identical.
 *
 * Four of the five are a declared catalogue: the export applies only the
 * eight-lobed one, to the 56×56 portraits of the guests. They are kept for the
 * same reason the five cycle colours are kept in colors.css — the design chose
 * them, and a comment is cheaper than rediscovering why they went missing.
 *
 * Whether to replace these with Material's own geometry is deliberately still
 * open: Google generates its shapes at run time from a rounded polygon and
 * publishes neither the paths nor the parameters, so it would mean depending on
 * somebody else's reconstruction. It is decided in PR 6, in front of a real
 * portrait — see docs/questioni-aperte.md. The `id`s would not change.
 *
 * The `<svg>` is zero-sized and hidden from assistive technology: it defines,
 * it does not draw.
 */
---

<svg width="0" height="0" style="position: absolute" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <defs>
    <clipPath id="clip-clover-4" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
      <circle cx="0.27" cy="0.27" r="0.27"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.73" cy="0.27" r="0.27"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.27" cy="0.73" r="0.27"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.73" cy="0.73" r="0.27"></circle>
      <rect x="0.27" y="0.03" width="0.46" height="0.94"></rect>
      <rect x="0.03" y="0.27" width="0.94" height="0.46"></rect>
    </clipPath>

    <clipPath id="clip-cookie-6" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
      <circle cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.36"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.5" cy="0.18" r="0.18"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.5" cy="0.82" r="0.18"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.22" cy="0.34" r="0.18"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.78" cy="0.34" r="0.18"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.22" cy="0.66" r="0.18"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.78" cy="0.66" r="0.18"></circle>
    </clipPath>

    <clipPath id="clip-clover-8" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
      <circle cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.275"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.5" cy="0.155" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.5" cy="0.845" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.155" cy="0.5" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.845" cy="0.5" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.256" cy="0.256" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.744" cy="0.256" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.256" cy="0.744" r="0.155"></circle>
      <circle cx="0.744" cy="0.744" r="0.155"></circle>
    </clipPath>

    <clipPath id="clip-gem" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
      <path
        d="M 0.6064 0.0704 L 0.7736 0.1496 Q 0.88 0.20 0.908 0.312 L 0.952 0.488 Q 0.98 0.60 0.9072 0.698 L 0.7928 0.852 Q 0.72 0.95 0.6024 0.9584 L 0.4176 0.9716 Q 0.30 0.98 0.2272 0.896 L 0.1128 0.764 Q 0.04 0.68 0.0456 0.5624 L 0.0544 0.3776 Q 0.06 0.26 0.1832 0.1928 L 0.3768 0.0872 Q 0.50 0.02 0.6064 0.0704 Z"
      ></path>
    </clipPath>

    <clipPath id="clip-slanted" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
      <polygon points="0,0.08 1,0 1,0.92 0,1"></polygon>
    </clipPath>
  </defs>
</svg>
